              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "город (górod) — \"a city, a town\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "город (górod) from Proto-Slavic gordŭ, \"an enclosure, a fort\" — inherited. Vasmer lists Lithuanian gardas, \"a fold\", Gothic gards, \"house\", and Sanskrit gṛhá-, \"house\": English yard is a cousin. Church Slavonic has град, \"city\", as in Петроград, \"Peter's city\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
